name: Telecom revenue assurance
tagline: "Completeness, re-rating, roll-forward and settlement controls over canonical synthetic telecom feeds"
description: "A revenue-assurance starter on canonical synthetic schemas (switch, mediated and rated usage xDRs, billed invoices, a tariff table, a prepaid balance ledger, interconnect rates and partner statements). Needs the Professional or Enterprise edition (Alert Rules). Controls: a 3-way switch-mediation-rating completeness Reconciliation with a lost-xDR Job, a rated-vs-billed Reconciliation, and sql.template Jobs for re-rating against the effective-dated tariff table, balance roll-forward (opening + in - out = closing) and interconnect settlement; leakage and data-quality findings land in separate Datasets with their own Alert Rules. Tolerances and thresholds are configuration. Reconciliation breaches open an Incident whose impact and Disposition feed the impact ledger. The synthetic golden corpus (fixed seed, planted leakages and benign look-alikes) lands in data/samples - copy each feed into data/inbox/<feed> to ingest. Runbooks: RUNBOOKS.md beside this file."
icon: heroicons_outline:scale
contents[7]: "8 Pipelines + canonical schemas", "2 Reconciliations", "4 control Jobs (sql.template)", "2 Alert Rules (leakage, data quality)", "2 Expectations", "Leakage + impact ledger Datasets", "Dashboard (leakage found / confirmed / recovered)"
